    "reference": "The Chesapeake Bay Bridge-Tunnel cost almost $200 million to increase the capacity of the above-water portion from 1995 to 1999. The bridge-tunnel carries U.S. Route 13 and provides a direct link between the Eastern Shore and South Hampton Roads regions. Motorists save 95 miles and 1/2 hour on a trip between Virginia Beach/Norfolk and points north and east of the Delaware Valley."
